8. AUTO JPG IMAGE BY SUBMIT — SETTINGS FEATURE

Add this exact setting:

Auto JPG Image by Submit

Description:

"Automatically generate a poster after every submission."

Use a modern toggle switch.

When ON

After every successful submission:

1. Save the TXT record first.
2. Confirm that the TXT record was saved.
3. Generate the corresponding JPG poster.
4. Save the poster inside the matching category folder.
5. Use the same RECORD_ID as the TXT record.
6. Update the poster generation status.

Example:

House submission:

TXT:
"House for Rent/2026-11-26.txt"

Poster:
"Generated Posters/House for Rent/House_000001.jpg"

Land submission:

TXT:
"Land for Sale/2026-11-26.txt"

Poster:
"Generated Posters/Land for Sale/Land_000001.jpg"

When OFF

- Save only the TXT record.
- Do not generate a JPG automatically.
- The user can later generate posters through Generated Files → Bulk Poster Generator.

Failure handling

If TXT saving succeeds but poster generation fails:

- Never delete or roll back the TXT record.
- Display:

"Property data saved successfully, but poster generation failed. You can retry."

- Provide a Retry Poster option.
- Preserve the record ID.
- Prevent duplicate posters when retrying.

If both operations succeed, display:

"Property saved and poster generated successfully!"

Important

- Save the toggle state persistently using SharedPreferences or an appropriate persistent settings mechanism.
- The toggle must remain in its previous state after the app is closed or restarted.
- Do not change TXT saving behavior when this setting changes.
- Run poster generation on a background thread.
- Never freeze the UI during image rendering.

