Performance requirements

The application must be designed to handle 1,000+ records, depending on available device storage and memory.

- Process records sequentially or in controlled batches.
- Do not load all full-resolution bitmaps into memory at once.
- Release each bitmap after saving.
- Avoid OutOfMemoryError.
- Keep the UI responsive.
- Support cancellation safely.
- Preserve completed posters if processing is cancelled.
- Allow failed records to be retried later.

Duplicate prevention

Before generating a poster:

- Check whether a valid poster already exists for the record ID.
- If it exists, skip it by default.
- Do not generate duplicate posters.
- Provide a clear count of skipped records.

If a user explicitly chooses to regenerate a poster, ask for confirmation before replacing the existing image.

