13. DATA INTEGRITY AND ERROR HANDLING

This is an offline data management application. Data safety is essential.

Implement the following safeguards:

- TXT must be saved before automatic poster generation.
- A failed JPG operation must never destroy a saved TXT record.
- Never overwrite daily TXT files.
- Preserve all existing records.
- Use unique record IDs.
- Prevent duplicate poster generation.
- Handle missing folders.
- Handle revoked SAF permissions.
- Handle insufficient storage.
- Handle malformed TXT records.
- Handle corrupted or incomplete images.
- Handle app interruption during bulk processing.
- Display clear, user-friendly error messages.

If an old TXT record cannot be parsed, do not silently discard it. Report the affected file or record and continue processing other valid records where safe.

Use reliable file operations and background execution for long-running tasks.

